course: dictionary
lesson: 11219
title: Wooden: made of wood, or stiff and without feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Wooden can mean made of wood, or it can mean stiff and without feeling. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «She put the hot pan on the wooden table.» Here wooden means made of wood, because the sentence is about a table and what it is made from. Put your meaning into the sentence to check: a table made of wood still makes sense.
explain: «His wooden smile did not reach his eyes.» Here wooden means stiff and without feeling. A smile made of wood would make no sense, so the clue is the smile not reaching his eyes. It looks like a smile, but it shows no real feeling.
fact: Wooden is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a wooden spoon or a wooden toy.
fact: «Wooden» means made of wood.
fact: «Wooden» also means stiff and without feeling, as in «a wooden expression».
fact: «Metals conduct heat well, so a metal spoon in hot soup gets hot while a wooden one stays cool.»
fact: The wooden horse of Troy is a legend, not a true story, so a good historian checks which stories are real.
exercise: «She sat down on the wooden chair.» What does wooden mean here? | *Made of wood | Stiff and without feeling | Very old and broken | Painted bright red
exercise: «His smile was wooden, and his eyes did not join in.» What does wooden mean here? | Shiny and wet | Made of wood | Very happy | *Stiff and without feeling
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Socks on smooth wooden stairs can slip» that tells you the stairs are made of wood. | *wooden | smooth | stairs | socks
test: «The wooden spoon stayed cool in the hot pan.» Why did the spoon stay cool? | It was put in cold water | *Wood does not conduct heat well | The pan had been turned off | Wood is always wet
test: Ella says, «Her answer was wooden, with no feeling at all.» What does wooden mean? | *Stiff and without feeling | Very hungry | Shiny and new | Made of wood
exam: Which meaning fits this sentence: «A wooden toy box sat under the window»? | Stiff and without feeling | Very old and wise | Short and rude | *Made of wood
